# Public addresses and domains that scripts/private-data-scan.py accepts.
#
# A domain entry also covers every subdomain (example.com covers app.example.com).
# An address entry is a single address or a CIDR block. Everything else that
# looks like a public address or a hostname fails the scan.
#
# Only add an entry that is public by nature: a documentation domain, an
# upstream vendor, a well-known resolver. A client's domain, a server the
# fleet runs on or an internal hostname is never allowed here; replace it in
# the tree instead.

